SUMMARY:Deadline: Go Short 2027: International Short Film Festival Nijmegen
  Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Go Short\, the international short film festival in Nijmegen\, 
 is open for entries for its 19th edition (6 to 11 April 2027). A small\, a
 pproachable Dutch festival that programmes fiction\, documentary\, animati
 on and experimental shorts.\n\nOrganisation: Go Short\, International Shor
 t Film Festival Nijmegen\nLocation: Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Compe
 tition open to films made in Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Ar
 rivals Competition for European film school projects.\nAward: Small submis
 sion fees per tier: EUR 12.50 (early bird\, 15 September 2026)\, EUR 15 (r
 egular\, 15 November) or EUR 20 (late\, 15 December) for films\; EUR 8/10/
 12 for video games\, VR/XR\, performances and installations\; EUR 7.50 fla
 t for music videos. Awards include the Go Short Award for Best European Sh
 ort\, Best Dutch Short\, the New Arrivals Award and an Audience Award (amo
 unts not published in the call).\nDuration: Festival 6 to 11 April 2027\n\
 nMore: https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-202
 7?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-2027?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Competition open to films made in
  Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Arrivals Competition for Europ
 ean film school projects.
END:VEVENT
